:: A Mocha to-do app: state is a list of task cords (0 = empty).
:: -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
:: This is the canonical shape of a MOCHA APP. A Mocha app is just a Latte `core`
:: that exposes two arms, and the Mocha runtime owns the (durable, syncable) state:
::   poke action state  -> (ok newstate)   a STATE TRANSITION (a write). The runtime
::                                          persists whatever `ok` wraps; the app is
::                                          pure — it never mutates, it returns the
::                                          next state.
::   peek query  state  -> value           a READ. Pure, returns a value derived
::                                          from state; never changes it.
:: `action` and `query` are cells: the HEAD is a tag atom (%add, %drop, %count …)
:: and the TAIL is its argument. `case tag of %x -> e ; ... ; _ -> e end` dispatches
:: on the tag (arms separated by `;`, `_` is the catch-all default). `ok x` is the
:: runtime's "transition succeeded, new state is x" wrapper. The same poke/peek +
:: tagged-action pattern recurs in lexicon.lat, editor.lat, and the chess apps.
import std
import mocha
core todo
  :: writes: add a task to the front, drop the task at an index, or clear everything.
  poke = fn [action state] ->
           let tag = head action in
           let arg = tail action in
           case tag of
             %add   -> (ok [ arg state ]) ;
             %drop  -> (ok (drop state arg)) ;
             %clear -> (ok 0) ;
             _      -> (ok state)
           end
  :: reads: how many tasks, the whole list, or whether a given task is present.
  peek = fn [query state] ->
           let tag = head query in
           let arg = tail query in
           case tag of
             %count -> (len state) ;
             %list  -> state ;
             %has   -> (member arg state) ;
             _      -> 0
           end
end
